Yet another suggestion to the dev team: add more special places to
the game. Every dungeon should have at least one dragon lair, where
dwelt a huge dragon of some kind. A golden one or whatever. However
the big nasty should be *a lot* harder to kill than anyone else of
his kind (I've also referred to a dragon as "he", don't mind). The
image of a big nasty dragon sleeping on a mount of treasures would
be a fine goal to an adventurer along the way to immortality.
 
So, whenever a person encountered the level where _the_ dragon dwelt,
he should get a message that informed about it somehow. "You smell
sulphur", "It seems to be rather fiery down here" and such would
serve as examples. 
 
This thing crossed my mind when a few weeks ago when I actually got
the amulet and gained immortality. Everything was very exciting until
I went to hell (well, that's how it is in real life, isn't it, too?)
where things got very boring. I didn't like at all the fact that I
had to search 20 maze levels for stairs (the wizard was easy to find).
10 levels of hell is enough if places like throne rooms, zoos, barracks
and so on appear more often. So the Medusa level should be around 40
or something. What do you think?
 
PS. All hobbits shouldn't speak of the One ring. Only Bilbo Baggins
should, and he should also wear a magical extra-lightweight mithril
coat and wield Sting. :-)
 
PPS. Hey, are there any other adventurers wandering in the dungeons?
I've never met one but that doesn't mean they couldn't exist. I'd
find it very realistic to meet a wizard or a priest along the way
to the depths of hell. 
